# 0.10.0

# IMPROVEMENTS:

-   implement soft delete for animals
-   validate adoption readiness and report missing requirements immediately
-   persist animal exit form data in frontend memory
-   add size and birth_date in variation report
-   add users management, roles and permissions
-   healthcare/shelter stage mechanism
-   track `in_shelter_from` on animals (new migration, auto-population on entries, manual move-to-shelter action)
-   expose healthcare vs shelter stage plus cat/dog filters in `AnimalSearchModel` responses
-   return entry types with `healthcare_stage` metadata for clients that drive form logic
-   add `/animals/{animal_id}/move_to_shelter` endpoint to flip shelter stage under `EDIT_ANIMAL`
-   animal image gallery with upload, delete, and set-profile-image; stored on a dedicated S3 bucket
-   therapy management: create, view, end, and soft-delete therapies; attach prescription and transport documents
-   therapy reminders card on the homepage showing active therapies with upcoming due dates
-   serve animal documents via S3 presigned URLs; bucket can be kept fully private
-   document download endpoint is now authenticated and enforces `DD` permission and per-kind `can_view` rules
-   presigned URL expiration configurable via `STORAGE__S3__PRESIGNED_URL_EXPIRES_IN` (default 600 s)
-   S3 and disk storage settings are now independently optional; only the selected backend needs to be configured
-   animal statistics endpoint and homepage card with period and structure filters
-   animal search and list support filtering by multiple structures simultaneously
-   move-to-shelter action requires selecting the target structure explicitly
-   PDF report for the current animal list search results
-   adopter search extended with city and phone filters; filter state persisted in session storage
-   city-code access control: users restricted to assigned cities on days and entries reports
-   `BAE` (Browse Animal Events) and `UAI` (Upload Animal Image) permissions added
-   Italian locale enabled for PrimeReact date/calendar components

# FIXES:

-   fix adopter creation bug
-   ensure `/users/` listing route matches FastAPI expectations
-   pin `bcrypt` to 4.3.0 to avoid upstream regressions
-   animal list report template: margins, footer positioning, table styling
-   custody report template: exit date variable name
-   PrimeReact filter panel button spacing

